Subject: [PATCH] net: implement shared eCash Merklix peer reconciliation

Add constructor-injected V2PeerProtocolHandler supporting merklixsync,
getmerklixbuck, merklixbuck, getshorttx, and shorttx across reconciliation scopes.

Original-Commit: 92f36b6549643e68cfdff30cd08c5f48f12acc16
Original-Patch: ecash/010
Split-Concern: whole

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Repair: Complete protocol build/PeerManager dispatch/lifecycle/GETDATA serving and validated serial admission/relay at their first owner. Reject V2-style roots in legacy eCash headers while retaining positional Merkle fast matching; native before/after regressions cover explicit/speculative candidates and requested sealed-header serving. Move later broadcast/batch/proactive-push assertions verbatim to their purposeful owners (test-redistribution.json), and track future batch/V2 capability upgrades in purpose-redistribution.json.

Plan-v2 owner repair: B1: overlay reconstruction does not confer checked Merkle provenance.

